WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:07.640
How in the world did our nation's economic
advisers go from ridiculing tariffs and subsidies-

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:11.920
Trade protectionism would be one of the stupidest
things we could possibly do.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.580
It was one of the causes of the Great Depression.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.020
To promoting pure protectionism.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:22.420
The steel industry must be kept aloft despite
the fact that it's always getting help.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:24.140
You know what I would do?

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:25.640
I would subsidize it.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:31.060
The answer lies in the paradigm shifting,
reality distorting and frequently cringe inducing power

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:32.580
of power itself.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.180
I hear something, it's Ronald Reagan rolling
over in his grave!

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.680
What are you talking about!?

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.040
It's a revolutionary thought-

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.680
My fellow Americans, it's sometimes said

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:47.489
that if you put three economists in a room
and ask them a question

00:00:47.489 --> 00:00:50.000
you're liable to get more than three answers.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.940
This is the sad story of a team of presidential
advisers with two opinions for every man.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:58.260
Before Trump took office they stood for a
principle that conservatives,

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:01.200
at least rhetorically, have championed for
decades.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.440
Free and fair trade brings growth and opportunity
and creates jobs

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:09.880
and they all warn that high trade barriers,
what is often called protectionism,

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.760
undermines economic growth and destroys jobs.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:15.480
Following in this tradition was Mike Pence.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:20.540
You can see that our existing trade agreements
have truly benefited Indiana

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:22.380
and the entire United States.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:24.420
As a member of the House of Representatives

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:27.329
Pence voted to normalize trade regulations
with China,

00:01:27.329 --> 00:01:30.860
he praised NAFTA, voted for the Central American
Free Trade Agreement,

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:34.620
supported the Trans Pacific Partnership and
backed free trade agreements

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:37.960
with Australia, Singapore, Chile and Peru.

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.280
I did not come to Washington to ask working
Americans

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.100
to subsidize the bad decisions of corporate
America.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.900
Even though Pence represented a state with
over a hundred thousand auto workers

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:51.800
he voted against then president Obama's corporate
bailouts out of principle.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:58.240
Donald Trump will choose Indiana Governor
Mike Pence to be his running mate.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.640
After joining team Trump, Pence was a changed
man.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.080
Rescued from an unpopular governorship, Pence
was thrust into the national spotlight

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:10.340
and his political career was given a new life.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:13.620
His conversion to protectionism was so sudden
and complete

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:17.080
he had a hard time convincing journalists
his new faith was sincere.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.320
So are you for the 35% tariff?

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.280
Let me go back to the intervening part.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.940
Are you for the tariff though for the-

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:27.840
The carrier, well I'm for us putting everything
on the table in negotiations

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.480
in renegotiating NAFTA.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.760
You're supporting the Trans Pacific Partnership

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:36.200
that Mr Trump says would rape this country.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.819
As Pence hit the talk show circuit

00:02:37.819 --> 00:02:41.569
we learned that every free trade agreement
he had supported his entire political career

00:02:41.569 --> 00:02:44.909
was now a bad deal and up for renegotiation.

00:02:44.909 --> 00:02:47.100
I support free trade and so does Donald Trump.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.340
Not really-

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:48.960
I do-

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.600
The United States under successive administrations
has been negotiating really bad trade deals-

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.120
A month before he was sworn in as Vice President

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.940
Pence went from badmouthing banking bailouts

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:02.300
to bankrolling the Carrier corporation in
his home state.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:05.300
Just one year after supporting free trade
with China

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.860
he now declared it enemy number one.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:12.969
China is not an ally, China is an adversary
of the United States.

00:03:12.969 --> 00:03:16.560
At about the same time Trump's campaign adviser
Stephen Moore

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.880
and White House Chief of Staff Reince Priebus

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:23.000
were stressing key elements of protection
in their speeches and public appearances.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.980
Donald Trump wants to bring jobs back from
overseas

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:29.860
and hold companies who want to send them abroad
accountable.

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:31.960
We should not have free trade with China

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:35.560
if they're going to continue to steal five
hundred billion dollars a year from us, right?

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:38.660
Moore told a group of top Republicans that
the GOP

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:41.880
was no longer the party of Ronald Reagan.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.160
The bedrock undernea th the Republican party

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:59.920
is shifting at the rate of one presidential
adviser at a time.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:03.200
After a year in office, members of Trump's
economic team

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:06.180
have either adopted the Commander in Chiefs
line on trade-

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.940
Tariffs are important to preserve the steel
industry.

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:12.440
Kept a low profile, or have resigned.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:17.520
This is Gary Cohn's last meeting in the cabinet
and of the cabinet

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:22.860
and he's been terrific, he may be a globalist
but I still like him.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:26.940
As the United States follows other countries
down the path of economic nationalism

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:29.900
advocates for free trade are losing their
voice.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:32.979
Fewer are making a compelling public case
for free trade

00:04:32.979 --> 00:04:35.310
as Milton Freedman did for decades.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:38.840
You know let's suppose three of us are out
in a boat in the ocean.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:43.040
And one of the fellas out there takes out
a gun and shoots holes in the bottom of the boat.

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:45.540
Is it the sensible thing for the others of
us to do

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:49.300
to take out our guns and shoot more holes
in the bottom of the boat?

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.180
That's kind of a silly notion isn't it?

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:56.840
But yet that is exactly the notion of protection
and retaliation.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:01.240
Which are the same arguments that Moore, Preibus,
Kudlow and Vice President Pence

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:04.420
all made before joining team Trump.

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:08.980
And as Ronald Reagan believed only inconsistently
during the 1980s.

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:13.860
This legislation will enable us to enforce
steel export restraints,

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:18.040
guard against unfair import surges into the
American market

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:22.580
and help keep the United States from becoming
the world's steel dump.

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:25.700
Although NAFTA and the precursor to the World
Trade Organization

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:27.340
were born from his administration,

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:32.440
Reagan also raised a punitive 100% tariff
on Japanese electronics,

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:35.340
a 45% tariff on Japanese motorcycles,

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:40.840
he slapped export quotas on cars and machine
tools and Canadian lumber and sugar.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:45.480
Just enough economic nationalism to make our
current protectionist in chief proud.

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:48.520
Frankly Ronald Reagan, I loved his style,
his attitude,

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:53.760
he was a great cheerleader for our, for you
know the country but not great on the trade.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:57.560
All of which is to say maybe President Trump
is more Reagan-esque

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:59.479
than even he gives himself credit for.

